fix(input): stop the pause status from stacking (autowrap)

The status line was padded to the FULL terminal width (cols), which triggers
autowrap on Tabby / iTerm / Windows Terminal: the cursor wraps to the next
line, the following erase moves to the wrong row, and the next frame is drawn
one row lower — the operator sees the "pause Ns" line duplicated/stacking.

The padded status+context row now keeps one column free (effective width
cols-1), so it never reaches the right edge and never autowraps. This is the
root cause of the pause-line duplication; it only appeared once the token
context started sharing the status row.

Add test/no-stack-render.test.ts: the padded row must never equal the terminal
width, and the editor must print a status row narrower than the terminal.
